{
    "map": {
        "additional_id_fields.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the additional unique ID field type and the fields that will be added to the output feature.</p><p>Use the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Unique ID</span> type when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Phone Records Table</span> parameter value has a unique identifier for all cell sector antennas. Use a combination of other <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">ID Type</span> values when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Phone Records Table</span> parameter value does not contain a universal unique identifier for all cell sector antennas.</p><ul><li>ID Type—The field name to be included in the output feature classes.</li><li>Field—The name of the fields that uniquely identify the cell sector antennas. These will be added to the output feature class.</li></ul><p><span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">ID Type</span> options are as follows:</p><ul><li>Unique ID—Uniquely identifies a cell sector antenna</li><li>Site ID—Uniquely identifies a cell site</li><li>Sector ID—Uniquely identifies a cell sector</li><li>Switch ID—Uniquely identifies a wireless network switch</li><li>LAC ID—Uniquely identifies the Location Area Code</li><li>Cascade ID—Uniquely identifies the sector in the wireless network cascade</li><li>Cell ID—Identifies the sector within an Location Area Code</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "additional_id_fields.domain.item1.CASCADE_ID": "Cascade ID",
        "additional_id_fields.domain.item1.CELL_ID": "Cell ID",
        "additional_id_fields.domain.item1.LAC_ID": "LAC ID",
        "additional_id_fields.domain.item1.SECTOR_ID": "Sector ID",
        "additional_id_fields.domain.item1.SITE_ID": "Site ID",
        "additional_id_fields.domain.item1.SWITCH_ID": "Switch ID",
        "additional_id_fields.domain.item1.UNIQUE_ID": "Unique ID",
        "additional_id_fields.dt.title1": "ID Type",
        "additional_id_fields.dt.title2": "Field",
        "additional_id_fields.title": "Additional Cell Sector ID Fields",
        "convert_utc.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the start and end date and time of the input records will be converted to the time zone of the local system or will remain in coordinated universal time (UTC).</p><ul><li>Checked—The start and end date and time of the input records will be converted from UTC to the time zone of the local system.</li><li>Unchecked—The start and end date and time will not be converted. This is the default.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "convert_utc.title": "Convert UTC Dates to Local Time Zone",
        "description": "Imports cell phone records from wireless network providers and associates those records with a cell site and sector feature classes as generated by the Cell Site Records To Feature Class tool based on identifier fields.",
        "destination_field.descr": "The field in the input table that contains the phone number or identifier of the callee.",
        "destination_field.title": "Destination Phone Number Field",
        "duration_field.descr": "The field in the input table that contains the duration of the phone call in seconds.",
        "duration_field.title": "Duration Field",
        "end_time_field.descr": "The field in the input table that contains the end date and time of the phone call or data event.",
        "end_time_field.title": "End Date and Time Field",
        "end_timing_distance_field.descr": "The field in the input table that contains the timing advance distance at the end of the call.",
        "end_timing_distance_field.title": "End Timing Advance Distance Field",
        "id_fields.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the unique ID field type and the fields that will be added to the output feature.</p><p>Use the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Unique ID</span> type when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Phone Records Table</span> parameter value has a unique identifier for all cell sector antennas. Use a combination of other <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">ID Type</span> values when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Phone Records Table</span> parameter value does not contain a universal unique identifier for all cell sector antennas.</p><ul><li>ID Type—The field name to be included in the output feature classes.</li><li>Field—The name of the fields that uniquely identify the cell sector antennas. These will be added to the output feature class.</li></ul><p><span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">ID Type</span> options are as follows:</p><ul><li>Unique ID—Uniquely identifies a cell sector antenna</li><li>Site ID—Uniquely identifies a cell site</li><li>Sector ID—Uniquely identifies a cell sector</li><li>Switch ID—Uniquely identifies a wireless network switch</li><li>LAC ID—Uniquely identifies the Location Area Code</li><li>Cascade ID—Uniquely identifies the sector in the wireless network cascade</li><li>Cell ID—Identifies the sector within an Location Area Code</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "id_fields.domain.item1.CASCADE_ID": "Cascade ID",
        "id_fields.domain.item1.CELL_ID": "Cell ID",
